+verdict: don't merge
+issue_repro: fail
+branch_tests: pass
+test_checks_the_fix: no
+
+The branch joins CRLF-split quoted lines into one row, but it does not remove
+the `\r` left before the closing quote. On `ISSUES/42-export.csv` the repro
+returns 3 rows, yet the second row's note is `call back\r\nafter 5pm"\r`
+instead of `call back\r\nafter 5pm`; the header field is `note\r` too.
+Splitting on `"\n"` keeps `\r` at each physical line end, so `strip('"')`
+cannot remove the closing quote.
+
+The new test only feeds LF input (`'1,"a\nb",x\n'`). It fails on main for that
+LF case, but it never exercises the CRLF export from the issue and passes while
+the reported repro fails, so it would not catch the actual bug. Its second
+assertion (`rows('1,"x, y",z\n') == [["1", "x", " y", "z"]]`) also locks in
+incorrect comma-inside-quotes splitting, so the test does not validate CSV
+behavior for the reported export format. The branch's own suite passes (2 tests).
